// REJECTS: Unexpected token '}'. Valid alternatives: ['generationElement']
//
// A generationNode is `{ (nodeId)? generationElement }` -- ORDERED, with the id optional and
// the element mandatory. Unlike almost every other body in these grammars this is not an
// unordered `( ... )*`, so the requirement is expressed by the rule itself and the message
// arrives at the closing brace.
//
// Worth pinning precisely because it is the exception: a rewrite that applies the house
// style -- collect clauses, validate afterwards -- gets a different message here, and gets
// `{ generationElement: x; id: 'y'; }` wrong in the other direction.
###GenerationSpecification
GenerationSpecification fixture::neg::NodeWithoutElement
{
   generationNodes: [
      {
         id: 'onlyAnId';
      }
   ];
}
